===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=over|inh|enm>on>over|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|on}}, from {{inh|en|ang|on}}, {{m|ang|an||on, upon, onto, in, into}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*ana}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*ana||on, at}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₂en-}}.

Cognate with {{cog|frr|a||on, in}}, {{cog|stq|an||on, at}}, {{cog|fy|oan||on, at}}, {{cog|nl|aan||on, at, to}}, {{cog|nds|an||on, at}}, {{cog|de|an||to, at, on}}, {{cog|sv|å||on, at, in}}, {{cog|fo|á||on, onto, in, at}}, {{cog|is|á||on, in}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌽𐌰}}, {{cog|grc|ἀνά||up, upon}}, {{cog|sq|në||in}}; and from {{der|en|non|upp á}}: {{cog|da|på}}, {{cog|sv|på}}, {{cog|no|på}}, see {{m|en|upon}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# In the state of being [[active]], [[function]]ing or [[operate|operating]].
#: {{ant|en|off}}
#: {{ux|en|All the lights are '''on''', so they must be home.}}
# [[happen|Happening]]; [[take place|taking place]]; being or due to be put into action.
#: {{ux|en|We had to ration our food because there was a war '''on'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Some of the cast went down with flu, but the show's still '''on'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|That TV programme that you wanted to watch is '''on''' now.}}
#: {{ux|en|This is her last song. You're '''on''' next!}}
#: {{ux|en|Are we still '''on''' for tonight?}}
#: {{ux|en|Mike just threw coffee onto Paul's lap. It's '''on''' now.}}
#: {{ux|en|England need a hundred runs, with twenty-five overs remaining. Game '''on'''!}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{n-g|Of a person, used to express agreement to or acceptance of a proposal or challenge made by that person; most commonly with subject "you" (see ''[[you're on]]'').}}
##: {{ux|en|"Five bucks says the Cavs win tonight." ―"You're '''on'''!"}}
##: {{ux|en|If he wants a fight, he's '''on'''!}}
# Fitted; covering or being worn.
#: {{ux|en|Your feet will soon warm up once your socks are '''on'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was trying to drink out of the bottle while the top was still '''on'''!}}
# {{lb|en|postpositive}} Of a stated part of something, oriented towards the viewer or other specified direction.{{cln|en|adjectives commonly used as postmodifiers}}
#: ''The photograph shows the UFO side '''on'''.''
#: ''edge '''on''''', ''side '''on''''', ''end '''on''''', ''face '''on'''''
# {{lb|en|chiefly|UK|informal|usually negative}} Acceptable, appropriate.
#: {{ux|en|You can't do that; it's just not '''on'''.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=May 22 1998|author=Phoenix Gamma|title=If I was owned Nintendo...|newsgroup=alt.games.video.nintendo-64
|passage=This kind of over-packaging of goods is completely not '''on'''.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=August 12 2003|author=DAB sounds worse than FM|title=Gerg Dyke's Speech at Radio Festival|newsgroup=alt.radio.digital
|passage=so Simon Nelson saying on Feedback "we'd prefer it if everybody listened to digital radio via DAB" is completely not '''on''' at all.}}
# {{lb|en|often negative}} Possible; capable of being successfully carried out.
#: {{ux|en|He'd like to play the red next to the black spot, but that shot isn't '''on'''.}}
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{lb|en|informal}} [[destined|Destined]]; [[involved]], [[doomed]].
# {{lb|en|baseball|informal}} Having reached a [[base]] as a [[runner]] and being positioned there, awaiting further action from a subsequent batter.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2019-02-24|author=Chris Kennedy|title=Aggies Earn Series Win Over Yale in Sunday Finale|site=New Mexico State University Athletics|url=https://nmstatesports.com/news/2019/2/24/baseball-aggies-earn-series-win-over-yale-in-sunday-finale.aspx|text=With one out and no men '''on''', Tristen Carranza belted a ball to the opposite field for a solo home run to put the NM State deficit at just 2-1.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2019-04-06|author=Daniel Martinez-Krams|title=Baseball Falls Short in Game 2 of UCLA Series|site=The Stanford Daily|url=https://www.stanforddaily.com/2019/04/06/baseball-falls-short-in-game-2-of-ucla-series/|text=Although Stanford was outhit 15-6, the Cardinal stranded eight runners to UCLA's three, hitting just 3-15 with runners '''on''' compared to the Bruin's 9-22.}}
# {{lb|en|cricket}} Within the [[half]] of the [[field]] on the same side as the [[batsman]]'s [[leg]]s; the [[left]] side for a [[right-handed]] batsman.
#: {{syn|en|leg}} {{ant|en|off}}
#: ''The captain moved two fielders to the '''on''' side.''
#: ''Ponsonby-Smythe hit a thumping '''on''' drive.''
# {{lb|en|snooker|postpositive}} Of a ball, being the next in sequence to be potted, according to the rules of the game.
#: {{ux|en|If the player fails to hit the ball '''on''', it's a foul.}}
# {{lb|en|acting|drama|RPG}} Acting [[in character]].
# {{lb|en|informal|of a person}} Performative or funny in a wearying manner.
#: {{ux|en|He always has to be '''on''', it's so exhausting.}}
# {{lb|en|euphemistic}} [[menstruating|Menstruating]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Hollie Smith Netmums|title=You and Your Tween: Managing the years from 9 to 13|publisher=Hachette|isbn=9780755361137
|passage=It still gets in the way of her doing things like swimming, and she avoids sleepovers when she's "'''on'''".}}

